# "Whenever you cast an instant spell from your hand, it gains rebound" (CR 702.88a, 613.1f). Bot1 casts Ojer Pakpatiq on
# turn 1 off Mox Sapphire, Mox Pearl, Mox Jet and an Island, then on turn 3 casts Lightning Bolt (Mox Ruby) at Bot2: the
# trigger resolves first and the Bolt, which has no rebound of its own, is given it. It deals 3 and is exiled as it resolves
# instead of going to the graveyard. At Bot1's next upkeep (turn 5) Bot1 casts it from exile for nothing: 3 more damage. That
# cast was not from a hand, so Pakpatiq does not trigger and the Bolt is put into the graveyard as it resolves.

